/-!
# Witness tables for the column homology quotient

These are untrusted data definitions. Data.lean checks a contraction for a - 1,
its 12-dimensional section, and the two local generator actions. Orbit.lean checks
closure and reachability. The first 50 entries of column.json's fixed_basis are
displacements; its last 12 supply sectionCols. Extending these 62 vectors by
preimages of the first 50 gives the contraction and quotient projection.

Source: ImageBound/source/column.json and geometry.py. Original ATLAS matrices and
word program: R. A. Wilson, S. J. Nickerson and J. N. Bray, online ATLAS of Finite
Group Representations; see ImageBound/source/README.md and Model.Data. Only the
literal a acting on columns is used. qxCols and qyCols encode images of basis
columns, so decoding them as columns transposes the source quotient row tables.
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace Janko4.OuterReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.TwoCoreCentralizerData.Generation.OrbitGeometry.Coordinates

